# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production environment — loaded by `npm run build` and `npm run build:mobile`
# (both run Vite in `production` mode).
#
# Non-secret values only; this file is committed. Real secrets belong in the
# deploy environment or env/.env.production.local (git-ignored).
#
# Wi-Mall production hosts — note the hyphen. `wimall.com` is a different
# company's domain and must never appear here:
#   wi-mall.com          main site / customer storefront
#   vendor.wi-mall.com   this app (Wi-Vendor)
#   agency.wi-mall.com   agency dashboard
#   agent.wi-mall.com    agent web
#   api.wi-mall.com      backend API
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# wi-mall backend — all /api calls go here. Must end in /api.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.wi-mall.com/api

# Base URL where uploaded files are served (defaults to the API origin /uploads).
# VITE_FILE_BASE_URL=

# Origin of the customer-facing storefront (the `landing` app). REQUIRED on
# mobile as well as web: the storefront preview iframes (/preview/product/:id and
# /preview/store) and every share / copy link a vendor produces are built from
# it. This is the main site, NOT the API origin.
VITE_STOREFRONT_BASE_URL=https://wi-mall.com

# ─── Payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RESOLVED 2026-09-13 — LEAVE THIS UNSET. It is no longer waiting on infra input.
#
# Stripe is switched OFF on the backend, deliberately:  is
# absent from the deployed jovi-mall environment, and its absence IS the off
# switch (backend/docs/DEPLOY-DOKPLOY.md § What is not covered here). A
# publishable key is only ever half of a pair — setting one here would surface a
# card option in the billing UI whose other half does not exist, so the upgrade
# would fail after the vendor had chosen it.
#
# Unset is therefore the correct production value, not a gap: the billing UI
# offers mobile money only, which is what the platform can actually take.
# NotchPay and MyCoolPay carry real payments.
#
# When Stripe is genuinely switched on, the backend secret key goes in first and
# the pk_live_… value here second — in that order, so there is never a window
# where the UI offers what the server cannot complete.
#
# Read by the WEB build only. Billing is read-only on mobile (D2 / Phase 5), so
# the native bundle never mounts a Stripe surface — see env/.env.mobile.
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ─── Push notifications (FCM web push) ────────────────────────────────────────
# RESOLVED 2026-09-09 — `bingoo-22222` IS the production messaging project. It
# was previously flagged here as "needs infra input" on the assumption that a
# separate production project would be stood up; that decision was made the
# other way, and this one project serves every environment and all three apps.
# The name is historical, not a signal that these are throwaway values.
#
# It is also the project behind android/app/google-services.json, which
# registers com.wi_mall.vendor alongside com.wi_mall.agency and
# com.wimall.agent_app — so web push and native push share a sender.
#
# When ANY of these is unset, push stays inert and in-app notifications continue
# to work. Keep them in sync with the hardcoded config in
# public/firebase-messaging-sw.js — a service worker cannot read Vite env vars,
# so that file is a SECOND copy of these values and drifts silently: a mismatch
# lets registration succeed and then delivers nothing.
#
# Web only. P2.6 switches this whole transport off inside a native shell, and
# native push is configured by android/app/google-services.json in P4.1.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBEm8btwePIHHYpSs41zebr6KmHIuWinA0
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=bingoo-22222.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=bingoo-22222
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=741831724264
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:741831724264:web:6741494f37bd0bd0d34d5d
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=BCnGJqU4hsphcmSNMlMUuwcKIDbvKXIU8lF85ylFCkIgrLbBOE9G6-Idq5xVhiFWbY_DdGmLUZSc309gBZo5-gA